# report/: the paper

`report.pdf` is built with pdflatex from `report.tex`, `references.bib` and `neurips_2026.sty` (the official
NeurIPS 2026 style file, unmodified, from
https://media.neurips.cc/Conferences/NeurIPS2026/Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026.zip, identical to venue-repo
`template/`). It uses the default anonymous submission mode, and the whole PDF is at most 2 pages, references
included. The NeurIPS checklist is omitted, as venue-repo decided, and the paper says so.

## Build

From this directory, once the delivery is assembled:

```
latexmk -pdf report.tex      # TeX Live 2026: pdflatex + bibtex (plainnat)
```

The inputs come from the other positions' delivered paths:
`results/numbers.tex` (every number), `tables/table_results.tex` (the table) and `figures/fig_accuracy.pdf` (the figure).

