## Where each number comes from

No number in `report.tex` is typed by hand. Each is a macro from `results/numbers.tex`, which
`code/summarize.py` writes from `results/run_local/folds.csv` (identical to `results/run_ibex/folds.csv`),
`results/reproducibility.json` (from `code/compare_runs.py`) and `code/data/`.

| in the paper | macros | source |
|---|---|---|
| mean accuracy and corrected 95% interval per method | `\accLRMean/Lo/Hi`, `\accKNNMean/Lo/Hi` | `summary.json` main.lr / main.knn |
| paired difference LR−kNN, interval, p | `\accDiffMean/Lo/Hi`, `\diffCorrectedP` | `summary.json` main.diff_lr_minus_knn |
| naive interval of the difference (contrast) | `\accDiffNaiveLo/Hi` | same, `naive` |
| folds where LR is better / tied / worse | `\foldsLRBetter`, `\foldsTie`, `\foldsKNNBetter` | same |
| selected k: range, median, mode; the grid | `\kMin`, `\kMax`, `\kMedian`, `\kMode`, `\kGridMin/Max` | `summary.json` k_chosen |
| design: folds, repetitions, n_train/n_test, seed, t critical value | `\nFolds`, `\nRep`, `\nSplits`, `\nTrain`, `\nTest`, `\seed`, `\tCrit` | `code/cv_compare.py`, `summary.json` |
| data md5, number of duplicate rows | `\dataMDFive`, `\nDuplicateRows` | `code/data/iris.arff`, `code/data/openml_61_meta.json` |
| Ibex job, partition, node; identical yes/no; differing folds and predictions | `\ibexJobId`, `\ibexPartition`, `\ibexNode`, `\runsDifferingFolds`, `\runsDifferingPredictions`, `\nPredictionsCompared` | `results/reproducibility.json`, `results/run_ibex/slurm_53912439.log` |
| software versions | `\verNumpy`, `\verScipy`, `\verSklearn`, `\verPython`, `\verPythonIbex` | `results/run_*/run.json` |

The table's values (`tables/table_results.tex`) and the figure are computed by figtab-repo's scripts from
`results/folds_long.csv`; they agree with the macros above (checked at build time).

